~ start
if Global.daughter_dialogue_progress == 0:
	D: Oh?
	D: So the unsung hero comes crawling back to his cave unprepared to face the demons he left behind. 

	PC: (Oh crap, do I know this guy too???)

	D: Why are you here?

	PC: (Is this my sister? My mother? My twice removed cousin?)
	PC: Uh, nothing much. Cuz. 

	D: …

	PC: Uh, mum. Sis. 

	D: GTFO of my sight. 

	PC: (Can’t see her face but even I can tell she’s glaring at me.)
	$> Global.daughter_dialogue_progress = 1
	=> END
if Global.daughter_dialogue_progress == 1:
	if Global.has_teddy_bear == true:
		PC: Is this yours?

		D: What!? Where did you get that??
		D: I mean- 
		D: No! Who would want that piece of trash! 
		D: You think I’m a baby who sucks on their thumbs?

		PC: Uh…

		D: You do!

		#Flashback
		$> Global.fade_in()
		$> Global.show_memorabilia("teddy_bear")

		PC: And that’s how Sir Woodsworth slew the great beast of Quagshire and saved his hometown. 
		PC: The end. 

		D: That’s it? But what about Sir Woodsworth’s squire who got lost in the swamp? 
		D: Also, what’s a squire? 

		PC: Well, some questions will have to be left unanswered sometimes. 
		PC: I’m sure Sir Woodsworth’s squire made it out of the swamp safe and sound. 

		D: And if he didn’t?

		PC: That…sure is a possibility…?
		PC: Anyways, it’s past your bedtime. 
		PC: I’ll tuck you in, okay?

		D: Can you give me {{Global.teddy_bear_name}}? 

		PC: Of course. 

		PC: Goodnight sweetie.

		$> Global.hide_memorabilia()
		$> Global.fade_out()
		#Flashback end
		
		$> Global.daughter_dialogue_progress = 2
		=> END
	else:
		D: GTFO of my sight. 

		PC: (Can’t see her face but even I can tell she’s glaring at me.)
		=> END
if Global.daughter_dialogue_progress == 2:
	IA: You can't talk to her! Her dialogue isn't finished being written yet!
=> END